P-8 (spec 017, the night shift; plan.md §10; tasks.md T070): tools/gates/toolchain_check.py checks the night images'
Claude Code pin.

What it changes:
  - deploy/night-shift/images/pins.json pins one Claude Code for every night image: claude_code, which the toolchain
    image's CLAUDE_CODE_VERSION build argument repeats. Beside a .devcontainer/toolchain.vars (make toolchain-check's,
    and the gate's export's, which the gate passes), the check adds a row, "claude code (night images)", held to the
    floor the installed Claude Code is (ADR 0023): at the floor or in its series OK, newer WARN (a row and a "WARN:"
    line that don't fail), older DRIFT. A file that can't say one version (the two disagree, no argument, not a
    version, not JSON) is DRIFT. No row while the file is absent, so main before the night shift's merge is unchanged.
    H4_NIGHT_PINS names another file; a pins file anywhere but a repository's .devcontainer/ gets no row, so the
    existing tests' scratch pins files are unaffected.
  - tools/gates/test/test_toolchain_check.py: eight tests (the floor, five malformed files, no file, where the pins sit,
    main end to end, and the repository's own pins.json once it exists); the host fixture clears H4_NIGHT_PINS.

On today's branch, pins.json says 2.1.322 and toolchain.vars' floor is 2.1.296, so the row is WARN, as the host's own
claude code row is: the gate's toolchain step is WARN, not FAIL. Moving the floor to 2.1.322 clears both, and runs the
agent-config evals again (the pin is in their trigger hash).

Spec IDs: tasks.md T002 ("The pins are read by install.sh and checked by P-8"), research.md R-16's pin.

Needed for: the merge.

How to apply, on your own branch, from the repository's root (one line each):
  B=feat/017-g5-patches
  F=docs/merge-requests/2026-11-12-feat-017-p8.patch
  git show "refs/heads/$B:$F" > /tmp/p8.patch
  sha256sum /tmp/p8.patch
  patch -p1 --dry-run < /tmp/p8.patch
  patch -p1 < /tmp/p8.patch

Verified on a fresh `git archive refs/heads/main` export (main d4870ec8): dry run and apply clean; `pytest
tools/gates/test/test_toolchain_check.py`: 29 passed, 1 skipped (the repository's pins.json isn't on main yet). With
the branch's deploy/night-shift/images/pins.json copied into the export: 30 passed; and the check itself printed
"claude code (night images)  2.1.296  2.1.322  WARN" beside the host's own claude code row.

